WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.229
A C N C router is a robot that moves a spinning bit to carve wood and plastic. Here's how it works.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.626
It moves in three directions.

00:00:10.626 --> 00:00:16.458
X is left and right along the gantry. Y is front and back. And Z is up and down.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:21.530
The spindle spins the bit up to twenty four thousand times a minute.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:26.360
Sharp flutes slice off tiny chips, and the dust shoe and vacuum suck them away.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:32.092
Before it carves, the machine needs to know exactly where your material is.

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:35.620
The Z probe finds the top surface. That's Z zero.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.021
Then you jog to the corner and set X and Y zero.

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:44.608
The bit cuts a little deeper on each pass, until it reaches the depth you set.

00:00:44.608 --> 00:00:49.652
Tabs are small bridges that hold the part in place, so it can't break free at the end.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:57.490
Clamps hold the material flat. Put them outside the cut path, where the bit and dust shoe can't hit them.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.129
Wear safety glasses and hearing protection. Tie back long hair and loose sleeves.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:07.551
Keep your hands out until the spindle has completely stopped.

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:11.122
And know where the E-stop is. One press stops everything.
